# Jlt has no subtyping: the grammar has no base clause and no derived-to-base
# conversion, and a value is known by its concepts, not by a class it derives
# from.  A class with a base that is not an empty class, or with a virtual
# function, is a finding.  An empty base is a registration spelled by
# inheritance (`struct is_x<T> : std::true_type`), read as the fact it
# states; a dependent base is judged by its template's primary definition.
tool inheritance
